Termination
(20)
Pre-Retirement Contracts may be terminated by:
the nominated end date of the Pre-Retirement Contract;
resignation by the staff before expiry of the Pre-Retirement Contract;
by mutual agreement between the parties;
unsatisfactory performance, serious misconduct, medical grounds, abandonment of employment or frustration of the employment contracts; or
redundancy.
(21)
Staff entering into a pre-retirement contract do so on the proviso that they will not be re-employed on a full time, fractional or fixed term position at the completion of a Pre-Retirement Contract.

Applications
(30)
Staff considering making an application should initially discuss the matter with their manager.
(31)
Applications should then be submitted through either the Dean, Executive Director, Deputy Vice Chancellors or the Provost.
(32)
Applications in writing (via email) must include the following details:
full name;
present position, date first occupied and present salary;
date of proposed conversion to a Pre-Retirement Contract;
date of proposed end of Pre-Retirement Contract;
proposed negotiable options to be offered;
proposed paid outside work, including anticipated income (if applicable);
proposed percentage to be worked (if applicable);
proposed re-allocation of duties within the school (if applicable).

Section 5 - Definitions
(35)
For the purpose of this Procedure:
Continuing staff member means a staff member with continuing employment;
Pre-Retirement Contract is a full-time or a part-time staff declaring that it is his or her intention to retire, a fixed-term contract expiring on or around the relevant retirement date may be adopted as the appropriate type of employment for a period of up to five years;
Substantive salary is a staff member’s base salary plus any additional allowances or loadings that are paid in connection with the position held.
